    <exercise number="57" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Explore and discuss the graphs of $$f(x) = \log_{\frac{1}{2}}(x)$$ and $$g(x) = - \log_{2}(x).$$ Make a conjecture based on the result.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>The graphs of $$f(x)= log 1 2 ( x ) f(x)= log 1 2 ( x )$$ and $$g(x)=- log 2 ( x ) g(x)=- log 2 ( x )$$ appear to be the same; Conjecture: for any positive base $$b\ne 1, b\ne 1,$$ $$log b ( x )=- log 1 b ( x ). log b ( x )=- log 1 b ( x ).$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
